## economy

The U.S. has a highly developed mixed economy[^18] that has been the world's largest nominally since about 1890.[^19] Its 2024 gross domestic product (GDP)[^20] of more than $29 trillion[^21] constituted over 25% of nominal global economic output, or 15% at purchasing power parity (PPP). The country ranks first in the world by nominal GDP,[^22] second when adjusted for purchasing power parities (PPP),[^23] and ninth by PPP-adjusted GDP per capita.[^23] In August 2026, the total U.S. federal government debt passed $40 trillion, having more than doubled in the previous decade.[^24] ([Economy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Economy))

